# CLAUDE.md — Frontend (SvelteKit)

Scope: `frontend/`, the SvelteKit app on Node. It reaches Laravel only over HTTP on the page's own origin; Caddy splits
the paths (root `CLAUDE.md`, Frontend).

## First frontend change

`frontend/` holds only this file until the first change that needs a page. That change creates the app. Steps 1–5 run
in the app container or on the host; on the host they need Node at the image's major and php. Step 6 needs docker:
without it, the rebuild and every `docker/e2e.sh` run are someone else's step (on the board, the `kanban` skill says
whose).

1. From the repo root:
   `npx sv@0.17.1 create frontend --template minimal --types ts --add tailwindcss="plugins:none" sveltekit-adapter="adapter:node" --no-install --no-dir-check`.
   No playwright add-on: the house setup replaces its demo routes, preview server and `playwright install`.
2. In `frontend/`:
   - `npm install`
   - `npm install -D --save-exact zod shadcn-svelte @playwright/test`
   - `npm install -D sveltekit-superforms bits-ui tailwind-variants cn@^0.3 tw-animate-css @lucide/svelte svelte-sonner @laravel/passkeys`
     `cn` takes the range the pinned registry's `utils` item declares (`^0.3` at shadcn-svelte 1.7.0).
<!-- if:reverb -->
   - `npm install -D laravel-echo pusher-js`
<!-- endif -->
3. The `check` script is
   `export PUBLIC_APP_URL=${PUBLIC_APP_URL:-http://localhost}; php ../artisan validation:export --check && svelte-kit sync && svelte-check --tsconfig ./tsconfig.json && playwright test --list --pass-with-no-tests > /dev/null`.
   The default only satisfies the type check outside the stack. `--list` loads every spec and the config without
   `globalSetup` or the `webServer`, so a spec that does not compile fails the check. No script runs
   `playwright install`.
4. `src/hooks.server.ts` with the `handle` in Guards, `/healthz` first. If
   `php artisan route:list --path=api/v1/auth/me` lists nothing, the same change adds the session probe and its
   `UserResource` (`routes/CLAUDE.md`, `app/Resources/CLAUDE.md`): `handle` calls it.
5. `vite.config.ts` per Config; `components.json`, `src/lib/utils.ts`, the CSS and `scripts/check-ui.mjs` per
   Components; `playwright.config.ts` per `tests/CLAUDE.md`, Browser flows.
6. Commit `package.json` and `package-lock.json`, then rebuild the stack (`up -d --build`): the entrypoint then runs
   `npm ci` and starts `vite`, and the image installs the browser for the `@playwright/test` pin (Hosting).
7. Boost detects JS packages only from a root lockfile, so it never installs its Tailwind skill for `frontend/`. Copy
   `vendor/laravel/boost/.ai/tailwindcss/4/skill/tailwindcss-development/` to `.ai/skills/tailwindcss-development/`
   and run `php artisan boost:update`.

## Stack

The packages in step 2, plus what the shadcn-svelte components declare (Components, Add), and nothing else without
the owner's approval (convention 6): SvelteKit 2 with Svelte 5 runes, adapter-node, TypeScript, Tailwind 4,
shadcn-svelte, superforms on `zod` 4, Playwright. HTTP is SvelteKit's `fetch` only. Icons come from
`@lucide/svelte` only, never emoji.

- The house runs the maintenance check of this set on each pin bump (laravel-project-setup `references/packages.md`).
  A package of the set that fails it in this project is a finding for the house, never a reason to swap it in a
  change.

- Every package is a devDependency: adapter-node bundles it into `build/`. One that must stay external (native code)
  goes in `dependencies`, which the prod image installs.
- Three are pinned exactly: `zod` (the parity proofs depend on its regexes; a bump reruns them), `shadcn-svelte` (the
  `ui/` gate) and `@playwright/test` (the image's browser matches it).

## Config

- Kit options live inline in `vite.config.ts`, top-level with no `kit:`:
  `sveltekit({ adapter: adapter(), csp: { … } })`. No `svelte.config.js` (ignored when the Vite config holds options).
- Keep the defaults Caddy relies on: `trailingSlash: 'never'` (`/about` is served from `about.html`), `appDir: '_app'`,
  no `paths.base`, adapter-node's `out: 'build'` and `precompress: true`.
- The dev server is `vite dev` on 127.0.0.1:5173 behind Caddy, started by the entrypoint. No `server.proxy`,
  `server.hmr`, `server.ws` or `host`; named hosts go in `server.allowedHosts` (`'.test'`), never `true`.
- Env:
  - server-only settings: `$env/dynamic/private` at runtime (`API_INTERNAL_URL`), reaching a page only through a
    server load;
  - what the browser or a prerendered page needs: `PUBLIC_*` from `$env/static/public`, baked in at build
    (`PUBLIC_APP_URL` = `APP_URL`), so the image is built per public URL. `vite dev`, `npm run check` and every
    build need it; Hosting supplies it;
  - never `$env/static/private`.
- No remote functions: the API is `/api/v1`, and form actions cover the rest.
- `src/app.d.ts` types `App.Locals`, `App.PageData` and `App.Error`.
- No SvelteKit route under `/api`, `/sanctum`, `/horizon`, `/up`, `/storage`, `/kanban` or `/healthz`: Caddy sends
  those paths elsewhere.
<!-- if:reverb -->
  Nor under `/app`, which is Reverb's.
<!-- endif -->

## Components: shadcn-svelte

`src/lib/components/ui/` is exactly what the pinned CLI writes and is never edited.

- **No `init`**: it calls a live endpoint that cannot be pinned, injects a font and re-pins `shadcn-svelte@latest`.
  Its outputs are project files, written once:
  - `components.json`: `"style": "vega"` (always explicit: an unknown style silently becomes another),
    `"typescript": true`, `tailwind.css` = `src/routes/shadcn.css`, aliases `$lib`, `$lib/utils`, `$lib/components`,
    `$lib/components/ui` and `$lib/hooks`, and `registry` =
    `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/huntabyte/shadcn-svelte/shadcn-svelte@<version>/docs/static/registry`, where
    `<version>` is the exact `shadcn-svelte` devDependency;
  - `src/lib/utils.ts`: the registry's `utils` item as the pinned CLI writes it (`cn` re-exported from the `cn`
    package, plus the types `WithElementRef`, `WithoutChild`, `WithoutChildren` and `WithoutChildrenOrChild`);
  - `scripts/check-ui.mjs` and its `check:ui` script (the gate, below).
- **CSS**: `src/routes/layout.css` is the one Tailwind entry, imported by the root layout. It imports, in this order,
  `tailwindcss`, `tw-animate-css`, `shadcn-svelte/tailwind.css`, `./shadcn.css` and `./theme.css`, then holds the
  house `@theme`.
  - `shadcn.css` is CLI-managed: no `@import "tailwindcss"`, only its `@theme inline`, `:root`/`.dark` and a
    hand-declared `@custom-variant dark (&:is(.dark *))`.
  - `theme.css` maps `--primary`, `--radius`, … in `:root` and `.dark` onto the house tokens. The CLI never touches it
    and it comes last, so an `add` rewriting `shadcn.css` changes nothing visible. House tokens never use shadcn's
    names (no `--color-primary`, `--color-background`, …).
- **Add** from `frontend/` with the pinned local CLI (`npx shadcn-svelte add <name> --no-deps-install`), only what a
  screen imports; remove a component nothing uses. Never `form` or `sonner`: they declare packages outside the set
  (Forms; toasts in SEO, UX and accessibility). Then `git diff package.json`:
  - a new entry is a package the component declares (`@internationalized/date` for the date pickers, …): choosing
    shadcn-svelte approved it, so `npm install` it;
  - a changed range on an existing entry goes back to the project's (the registry can name an older major);
  - review the rest of its diff as code.
- The project's UI layer lives in `src/lib/components/<area>/`, never in `ui/`: looks through the `class` prop (`cn`
  merges it last), variants through `tv({ extend: buttonVariants, … })`, behaviour through a wrapper component.
- **Update**: bump the pin, the registry tag and `cn`'s range (the new `utils` item's) together, rerun
  `add <every installed component> --yes --overwrite`, commit `ui/`. Generated code failing `npm run check` means
  another pin (ask the owner), never an edit.
- **The gate is `npm run check:ui`.** It fails unless `components.json` names the pinned tag and sets `style`. Then,
  in a temp dir, it runs `npx shadcn-svelte@<version> add <every directory in ui/> --yes --overwrite --no-deps-install`
  and fails on any diff in `ui/`, printing it. The temp dir holds:
  - a `package.json` with only the project's `svelte` and `tailwindcss` ranges (no `@sveltejs/kit`, so the CLI skips
    `svelte-kit sync`);
  - a `tsconfig.json` mapping `$lib` and `$lib/*` to `./src/lib`;
  - copies of `components.json` and the CSS files.

  It needs the registry host, so it is not in `npm run check`. Run it before a push touching `ui/`, `components.json`
  or the pin, and after every update.

## Forms

Laravel validates; the browser copy only gives fast feedback. Every form is sveltekit-superforms with shadcn's
`field` components.

- **Schemas come only from the export** (`app/Requests/CLAUDE.md`), committed and never edited:
  `import * as register from '$lib/validation/generated/register'`.
- **Adapters** come from `sveltekit-superforms/adapters`: `zod4(register.schema(locale))` on the server and for
  `defaults()`, `zod4Client(register.schema(locale))` as the client `validators`. Build `schema()` once per locale.
- `dataType: register.dataType`. It is `'json'` for nested objects, arrays of objects or arrays of arrays: the form
  then uses `use:enhance` and needs JavaScript. Arrays of primitives are repeated inputs. Arrays are never nullable
  in the schema: an empty one posts `[]` (`app/Requests/CLAUDE.md`).
- **A form posted to Node** is a form action, working without JS and calling `/api/v1` only.
  - `load` returns `{ form: await superValidate(zod4(…)) }`.
  - The action runs `superValidate(request, zod4(…))`: invalid input returns `fail(400, { form })`. Otherwise it calls
    Laravel with `event.fetch`. A 422 goes through the helper, then `fail(422, { form })`; success is `message()` or
    `redirect(303, …)`.
  - Upload fields (the schema strips them): read the body once, `const fd = await request.formData()`, run
    `superValidate(fd, zod4(…))`, take the files from `fd` and send them to Laravel as multipart.
- **A form that calls `/api/auth/*`** runs in the browser:
  `superForm(defaults(zod4(…)), { SPA: true, validators: zod4Client(…), dataType, onUpdate })`, where `onUpdate`
  calls Laravel through the browser client and maps a 422 with the same helper.
- **The 422 helper**, `applyLaravelErrors(form, errors, adapter)` in `src/lib/forms/laravel-errors.ts`, calls
  `setError` once per key:
  - branches come from `adapter.shape` (the full `zod4` adapter), never `form.shape` (undefined on a posted form);
  - dotted keys become superforms paths: `items.0.name` → `items[0].name`;
  - a key naming an object or an array (`items`, `address`, `items.3`) gets `._errors`;
  - a key outside the schema becomes a form-level error: `setError(form, '', messages)`.

  An array item's error renders from either shape, `string[]` or `{ _errors }`: superforms stores indexes 0–9 and 10+
  differently.
- Server-only rules (unique, exists, …) are listed at the top of each generated file and reach their field through
  the 422.
- Numeric fields are `<input type="number">`. Never spread `$constraints` onto inputs (a `pattern` loses its flags).
- **One field wrapper**, `src/lib/components/form/form-field.svelte`, takes the superform and a field `name` and
  wires the field:
  - `Field.Field` with `data-invalid` while the field has errors, `Field.Label for={id}`, and `Field.Description` and
    `Field.Error` with their own ids (`Field.Error` takes `{ message }[]`:
    `errors={msgs.map((message) => ({ message }))}`);
  - its `children` snippet gets the control's props: `id`, `name`, `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby` (the
    description and error ids). Every control spreads them: native inputs and the bits-ui controls (Select,
    Checkbox, Switch, RadioGroup) alike.
- **A custom input** (formatted number, date, `EntityPicker`, anything without a native control) posts through
  `<input type="hidden" name={…} value={raw}>` holding the raw value, never the formatted text. A field the page shows
  but does not post is a bug: an update then clears it. Its wrapper in `src/lib/components/<area>/` sits inside the
  field wrapper and carries the hidden input.

## API client

One module, `src/lib/api/client.ts`, takes the `fetch` it is given, so the same calls run on both sides
(`event.fetch` on the server, a load's `fetch` or `window.fetch` in the browser).

- Relative URLs, JSON bodies, and `Accept: application/json` on every call (Fortify answers JSON only then).
- Failures are typed: a 422 carries the `errors` bag, a 401, 403, 404, 409, 419 or 423 its status. Nothing is
  swallowed.
- A response header a universal load reads during SSR goes in
  `resolve(event, { filterSerializedResponseHeaders })`.

### Browser

- A mutating call sends `X-XSRF-TOKEN`, URL-decoded from the `XSRF-TOKEN` cookie; without that cookie it first calls
  `/sanctum/csrf-cookie` (`src/lib/api/csrf.ts`, browser-only).
- **Only the authoritative `GET /api/v1/auth/me` decides the session is gone.**
  - An incidental 401 or 419 elsewhere rejects to its caller untouched: a call raced after login never signs the user
    out.
  - On an authoritative 401 it calls `invalidateAll()` only when `page.data.user` was set, so a reload never loops.
  - It never navigates to `/login` itself; the server guards redirect.
- **`probeSession()`** makes the speculative `GET /api/v1/auth/me` calls, where a 401 is expected; a per-call flag
  stops it tearing anything down. Never decide by pathname: during a load, `page.url` is still the previous route.
- **Every sign-in settles the session before anything else runs** (login, the two-factor challenge, register,
  passkey login). After Laravel's success:
  1. `/sanctum/csrf-cookie` again, because the session was regenerated;
  2. ONE serial `GET /api/v1/auth/me`;
  3. `goto(target, { invalidateAll: true })`.
- Logout: `POST /api/auth/logout`, then `/sanctum/csrf-cookie`, then `goto('/login', { invalidateAll: true })`.

### Server: `handleFetch`

`handleFetch` in `src/hooks.server.ts` rewrites every same-origin `/api/v1/*` request to `API_INTERNAL_URL`, Caddy's
internal address (Hosting), and sets the headers itself (SvelteKit stops forwarding them once the host changes):

```
cookie            ← the browser request's Cookie header
X-XSRF-TOKEN      ← event.cookies.get('XSRF-TOKEN')
Origin            ← event.url.origin when the XSRF-TOKEN cookie is present; otherwise API_INTERNAL_URL's origin
X-Forwarded-For   ← the incoming X-Real-IP header, which Caddy sets in every tier
X-Forwarded-Host  ← event.url.host
X-Forwarded-Proto ← event.url.protocol.slice(0, -1)
X-Forwarded-Port  ← event.url.port || (event.url.protocol === 'https:' ? '443' : '80')
Accept            ← application/json
```

Never a `Referer`.

- **`Origin` decides whether the call is the browser's session.** The public origin is in `SANCTUM_STATEFUL_DOMAINS`;
  `API_INTERNAL_URL`'s host:port never is, so an anonymous render starts no Laravel session. Never leave `Origin`
  unset: SvelteKit then adds the public origin itself.
- **`API_INTERNAL_URL`'s origin never equals a page's origin**: SvelteKit would answer such a fetch itself (Hosting
  keeps the web port off 8080).
- **`Set-Cookie` from a call Node makes never reaches the browser.** Nothing that creates, regenerates or ends a
  session runs on the server, and no `/api/auth/*` or `/sanctum/*` call either.
- **API reads go in universal `+page.ts`/`+layout.ts` loads**: inlined during SSR, called from the browser on client
  navigation (keeping the session cookie alive). Server loads are for `locals`, secrets and guards.
- **No hairpin requests**: server code never `event.fetch`es a static file or a prerendered page; import the data.
- While prerendering (`building`), neither `handle` nor `handleFetch` calls Laravel.

## Auth pages

**Every `/api/auth/*` call goes from the browser, after `/sanctum/csrf-cookie`**: Laravel's `web` group fails the CSRF
check of an anonymous call from Node. These pages need JavaScript and say so in a `<noscript>`.

| Page | Calls |
|------|-------|
| `/login` | `POST /api/auth/login`; `{ two_factor: true }` → `/two-factor-challenge` |
| `/two-factor-challenge` | `POST /api/auth/two-factor-challenge` (a code or a recovery code) |
| `/register` | `POST /api/auth/register` |
| `/forgot-password` | `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` |
| `/reset-password/[token]?email=` | `POST /api/auth/reset-password`; the mailed link lands here |
| `/email/verify/[id]/[hash]?expires=&signature=` | `GET /api/auth/email/verify/{id}/{hash}` with the same query unchanged (the signature covers Laravel's `/api/auth/…` URL); the mailed link lands here |
| `/confirm-password?redirect=` | `POST /api/auth/user/confirm-password`, or a passkey; every 423 from Laravel leads here and back |

- **Confirmation** offers the password when `GET /api/v1/auth/me` reports `has_password`, a passkey when
  `passkeys_count` > 0, else "sign out and use Forgot password" (root `CLAUDE.md`, Auth).
- **Account settings** (profile, password, two-factor, passkeys) call `/api/auth/user/*`; a 423 leads to
  `/confirm-password`.
- **Redirect targets** from `?redirect=` are used only when they start with a single `/` (not `//`, not `/\`), else
  `/`, on the server and in the browser.
- **Social sign-in**, once built: the buttons come from `GET /api/auth/providers`, one link per provider,
  `<a href="/api/auth/{provider}/redirect" data-sveltekit-reload data-sveltekit-preload-data="false">`. `/login` shows
  `?social_error=<code>`. Linking calls `POST /api/auth/{provider}/link` and follows its `{redirect}`.
- **Passkeys.** `@laravel/passkeys` has no base-URL option, so `src/lib/auth/passkeys.ts` passes the routes:
  - register: `/api/auth/user/passkeys/options` and `/api/auth/user/passkeys`;
  - sign in: `/api/auth/passkeys/login/options` and `/api/auth/passkeys/login`;
  - confirm: `/api/auth/passkeys/confirm/options` and `/api/auth/passkeys/confirm`.

  The wrapper is browser-only, imported from event handlers.

## Guards, session state, statelessness

- **`handle`** in `src/hooks.server.ts` does three things, in this order:
  1. `/healthz` returns `new Response('ok')`, for the container healthcheck on 127.0.0.1:3000. It never reads the
     client address (with `ADDRESS_HEADER` set, that throws without the header) and never calls Laravel.
  2. Only when the request carries the `XSRF-TOKEN` cookie, `probeSession(event.fetch)` fills `event.locals.user`
     (`null` on a 401). An anonymous request makes no Laravel call.
  3. A response to a request that carried the session gets `Cache-Control: private, no-store`.
- **Route groups**: `(public)` for anyone; `(guest)` for the sign-in pages, which send a signed-in user away; `(app)`
  for signed-in users only.
- **The guard** is a server redirect in the group's `+layout.server.ts`: `redirect(303, '/login?redirect=…')`. Never
  `$effect`, `beforeNavigate` or `window.location`. It only steers navigation; `auth:sanctum` and the policies decide
  every call.
- **The user reaches components as `page.data.user`.** The root and the `(app)` `+layout.server.ts` both return
  `{ user: locals.user }`: a `locals`-only load does not rerun on client navigation, so without the second, a user
  arriving from a prerendered page keeps `user: null`.
- **Node is stateless**, as under Octane: no request or user data in module scope (no module-level `$state`, store or
  cache the server imports). Per-request data goes in `event.locals`.
- **Navigation** is one catalog, `src/lib/config/navigation.ts`, each item naming its permission (`null`: any
  signed-in user); `deriveNavigation(user)` filters it and drops empty sections.
- **Svelte 5 runes only.** `$effect` is for work outside Svelte (the DOM, a third-party widget), never to derive data
  or to navigate. Page state comes from `$app/state`.

## Rendering, prerendering, caching

- SSR is the default. **Prerender** only where the data exists at build time: the build stage has no Laravel or
  database, and a build never calls `/api`. Where that data comes from is a per-project decision on the board. Pages
  with form actions or reading `url.searchParams` are not prerendered.
- **A prerendered page is public**: the same for every visitor, no personal data. `handle` never runs for it.
- **Redirects** belong in SSR (`redirect()`) or Caddy, never a prerendered route (it becomes a 200 meta-refresh
  page).
- **Cache headers.** Caddy sets them for prerendered files and `/_app/immutable/*` (Hosting); a `setHeaders` during
  prerender only becomes a meta tag. An anonymous public SSR page sets
  `Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=…, stale-while-revalidate=…` and `Vary: Cookie` in its `load` (the root
  layout carries `user`, so the browser never reuses a signed-out copy). `handle` overrides it with `private, no-store`
  when the request carried the session.
- **Absolute URLs** (canonical, `og:url`, the sitemap) come from `PUBLIC_APP_URL`, never `url.origin`, which is
  `http://sveltekit-prerender` while prerendering.
- **Prefetch**: `data-sveltekit-preload-data="hover"` on `<body>` in `app.html`; no
  `data-sveltekit-preload-code="eager"` on listings. A link that leaves SvelteKit (`/api/*`, `/horizon`, a provider
  redirect) carries `data-sveltekit-reload` and `data-sveltekit-preload-data="false"`.
- No size or speed budgets and no Lighthouse gates: the practices here are the rule.

## Content Security Policy

`csp` sits in the `sveltekit({ … })` options with `mode: 'auto'`: SSR responses get a nonce header, prerendered pages
a `<meta>` with hashes.

```ts
csp: {
  mode: 'auto',
  directives: {
    'default-src': ['self'],
    'script-src': ['self'],
    'style-src': ['self', 'unsafe-inline'],
    'img-src': ['self', 'data:'],
    'font-src': ['self'],
    'connect-src': ['self'],
    'object-src': ['none'],
    'base-uri': ['self'],
    'form-action': ['self'],
    'frame-ancestors': ['none'],
  },
},
```

- **`'unsafe-inline'` is for styles only** (server-rendered `style=` attributes). Scripts never get it, nor
  `unsafe-eval`.
- **No inline script in `app.html`, never `%sveltekit.nonce%`** (any prerendered route fails the build). A script goes
  in a component or under `static/`.
- **`frame-ancestors` on prerendered pages**: a `<meta>` policy drops it, so Caddy adds `frame-ancestors 'none'` for
  prerendered files, and never a second full policy on SSR paths (Hosting).
- **New origins** (a CDN) are added here in the same commit as the code that needs them.
<!-- if:reverb -->
- **Reverb**: Echo connects to the page's own origin and Caddy sends `/app/*` to Reverb, so `connect-src 'self'`
  covers it.
<!-- endif -->

## SEO, UX and accessibility

- A public page's content is server-rendered, with real `<a href>` links; title, meta description and canonical come
  from `load` data, in `<svelte:head>`.
- `sitemap.xml` and `robots.txt` are `+server.ts` routes, prerendered when their data allows, otherwise SSR with
  `Cache-Control`.
- `{text}` is safe; `{@html}` only for the output of Laravel's `Markdown::render()`.
- **Never make users type identifiers.** Every entity reference is a searchable combobox, `EntityPicker`, backed by
  `GET {resource}/search` and `GET {resource}/autocomplete` (`term`, `limit`, optional id filters). A closed
  vocabulary uses a Select, never free text.
- **Shared building blocks**: one data table (server-side sort, filter, pagination, selection; bulk actions via
  `{resource}/bulk-action`), one confirm dialog before anything destructive, toasts for results that are not on the
  page, one wizard for multi-step flows.
- **Toasts** are `svelte-sonner`'s `Toaster`, once in the root layout, through `src/lib/components/app/toaster.svelte`:
  its `--normal-bg`, `--normal-text` and `--normal-border` from the popover and border tokens, `@lucide/svelte`
  icons, and `theme` matching the page's colour scheme (`light` while the app has no dark mode).
- **Never a blank pane.** SSR delivers the first data (realtime only updates it); client-side waits show skeletons
  of the final size. A failed load renders an error state: what failed, the server's message (a 429 says when to
  retry) and a retry action. Never nothing, never a silently empty list: every client-side fetch and `{#await}` has
  its failure branch.
- **The design reference.** When the owner has decided a visual reference (root `CLAUDE.md`, What we are building), a
  change that adds or changes a page names the reference section it implements, and one of its criteria compares a
  screenshot of the page with that section. A missing layout element fails it.
- **WCAG 2.1 AA, full keyboard navigation.** Dialog focus comes from bits-ui; an overlay opened by a global shortcut
  saves `document.activeElement` on open and restores it on close. Every interactive element has an accessible name;
  live regions announce dynamic changes. Contrast ≥ 4.5:1 for text, 3:1 for large text and UI. A skip link on every
  page. Svelte's a11y warnings are fixed, never silenced.
<!-- if:reverb -->

## Realtime

Channel auth, payload rules and operations are in `app/Events/CLAUDE.md` (Broadcasting).

- **Echo lives only in the browser**: `src/lib/realtime/echo.ts` creates it on first use after hydration, never at
  module scope on the server.
- **It connects to the page's own origin** (Caddy sends `/app/*` to Reverb): `wsHost` = `location.hostname`, `wsPort`
  and `wssPort` = `location.port` (or 80 and 443), `forceTLS` = `location.protocol === 'https:'`.
- **Only the key comes from the server**: the `(app)` layout's server load reads `REVERB_APP_KEY` from
  `$env/dynamic/private`. An empty key (the e2e run) means no Echo.
- **Channel auth** posts to `/api/broadcasting/auth` with the browser client's cookie, `X-XSRF-TOKEN` and
  `Accept: application/json`.
- **One reconnect spine.** `src/lib/realtime/connection.ts` binds the connection state once and exposes
  `onReconnect(cb): Unregister`, firing only on a true reconnect (a `connected` after a real drop, flaps debounced,
  never the first connect). `disconnectEcho()` clears it at logout. Every feature re-auths and backfills through it.
- **"Live" is refetch-on-event.** A list that can have gaps keeps a `(created_at, id)` watermark and on reconnect
  merges the gap from a keyset `…/since` endpoint, deduped by id (ids are random: `database/CLAUDE.md`). Deltas merge in
  place.
- **One setter per list** dedupes by id and sorts by `(created_at, id)` ascending.
- **Counters come from the server**: a broadcast carries the authoritative count; new arrivals are announced in a
  polite `aria-live` region.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- if:tenancy -->

## Tenancy

The tenant appears in a body only as the `_tenant` marker or the switcher's `tenant` (root `CLAUDE.md`, Tenancy).

- `handle` keeps `current_tenant` from `GET /api/v1/auth/me` in `locals.tenant`; the layouts pass it on as
  `page.data.tenant`.
- **`X-Tenant` on every call**, carrying the tenant the page was rendered for:
  - the browser client takes it from `page.data.tenant`;
  - every form renders `<input type="hidden" name="_tenant" value={page.data.tenant.id}>`; its action sets `X-Tenant`
    from it (the body read once, Forms), so a stale tab's post meets the 409;
  - `handleFetch` adds `X-Tenant` from `locals.tenant` only when the request carries none (SSR loads), never over the
    page's.
- **A 409 `tenant_changed`**: show "The tenant changed in another tab — reload" with a reload action. Never retry
  into the new tenant.
- **A 403 `no_tenant`** shows the project's no-tenant page.
- **The switcher** is a browser call, because it changes the session: `POST /api/v1/current-tenant` with `tenant`,
  then `invalidateAll()`.
- Prerendered pages and `public` caches never depend on a tenant. Browser storage keys include the tenant id.
<!-- if:reverb -->
- After a switch, call `disconnectEcho()`, then subscribe to the new tenant's channels (`tenant.{tenantId}.…`).
<!-- endif -->
<!-- endif -->

## Before a push

- Always `npm run check`, in the app container or on the host (First frontend change): it runs
  `validation:export --check` first, so it needs php.
- `npm run check:ui` when `ui/`, `components.json` or the `shadcn-svelte` pin changed.
- The Playwright flows and Pest tests the change touches (`tests/CLAUDE.md`).
